---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Space Marines Beginner's Guide — Warhammer 40k"
  description="New to Space Marines? Learn how they play, which Chapter to pick, how to paint them, and exactly what to buy first."
>

  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="px-6 pt-16 pb-12 border-b border-[#2a2a35]">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <a href="/factions" class="text-sm text-[#4a4855] hover:text-[#8a8590] transition-colors mb-6 inline-block">
        ← All Factions
      </a>
      <div class="flex items-start gap-6">
        <div class="text-6xl">⚔️</div>
        <div>
          <p class="text-[#c9a84c] text-sm font-semibold tracking-widest uppercase mb-2 font-display">Faction Guide</p>
          <h1 class="font-display text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-bold mb-4">Space Marines</h1>
          <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-lg max-w-2xl leading-relaxed">
            The face of Warhammer 40k. Genetically enhanced supersoldiers in power armor, 
            standing between humanity and everything that wants to destroy it. The most popular 
            faction in the game — and for good reason.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Quick stats -->
      <div class="mt-10 grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-4 gap-3">
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] uppercase tracking-wide mb-1 font-display">Playstyle</p>
          <p class="font-semibold text-sm">Versatile</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] uppercase tracking-wide mb-1 font-display">Painting</p>
          <p class="font-semibold text-sm text-yellow-400">Medium*</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] uppercase tracking-wide mb-1 font-display">Rules</p>
          <p class="font-semibold text-sm text-yellow-400">Medium</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] uppercase tracking-wide mb-1 font-display">Starter Cost</p>
          <p class="font-semibold text-sm">~$160–$230</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] mt-3 italic">*Painting difficulty depends on which Chapter you choose. More on that below.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Lore -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-6">Who are the Space Marines?</h2>
      <div class="text-[#b8b4c0] leading-relaxed space-y-4 text-lg">
        <p>
          In the grim darkness of the far future, humanity's greatest weapon is the Space Marine — 
          a warrior who was already exceptional before the process began. Recruits are taken young, 
          put through brutal trials, and subjected to surgical implantation of nineteen gene-seed organs 
          that reshape their bodies entirely. What emerges is no longer quite human.
        </p>
        <p>
          A Space Marine is seven feet of engineered killing machine. Their bones are reinforced, 
          their blood clots in seconds, they can spit acid, see in total darkness, and survive 
          wounds that would kill ten ordinary soldiers. They wear Mk X Tacticus power armor — 
          a walking tank that amplifies their already superhuman strength. They carry bolters 
          that fire self-propelled explosive rounds.
        </p>
        <p>
          They are organized into Chapters — independent armies of roughly 1,000 warriors, 
          each with their own culture, homeworld, colors, and identity. The Ultramarines follow 
          a rigid doctrine of tactical excellence. The Blood Angels carry a terrifying flaw 
          that drives them toward berserk fury in battle. The Space Wolves fight like Viking 
          berserkers and keep giant wolves as companions. There are over a thousand Chapters, 
          and choosing one is one of the most personal decisions in the hobby.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- Playstyle -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-6">How they play on the table</h2>
      <div class="text-[#b8b4c0] leading-relaxed space-y-4 text-lg mb-10">
        <p>
          Space Marines are the definition of <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">jack of all trades</strong>. 
          They shoot well. They fight well in melee. They're mobile. They're durable. 
          They're not the absolute best at any one thing, but they're competent at everything — 
          which makes them genuinely forgiving for new players.
        </p>
        <p>
          The army rewards smart positioning and target priority. Marines are expensive in points 
          (each model counts), so you need to be deliberate — but you're not micromanaging 
          thirty cheap models. A typical army might have 30–50 models total, which keeps the 
          cognitive load manageable while you're still learning the rules.
        </p>
        <p>
          Each Chapter has its own unique rules (called Chapter Tactics) that skew the playstyle. 
          Ultramarines are tactically flexible. Blood Angels want to get into melee. Dark Angels 
          have strong ranged firepower. This means two Space Marine players can have 
          completely different armies and experiences.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-5">
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold mb-3 text-green-400">Space Marines are for you if...</h3>
          <ul class="text-[#b8b4c0] text-sm space-y-2">
            <li>✓ You want the most iconic 40k faction</li>
            <li>✓ You want flexibility — shooting, melee, or both</li>
            <li>✓ You want a forgiving army to learn the game on</li>
            <li>✓ You want the most tutorials, guides, and community support</li>
            <li>✓ You want a faction with strong identity you can make your own</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-5">
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold mb-3 text-red-400">Maybe look elsewhere if...</h3>
          <ul class="text-[#b8b4c0] text-sm space-y-2">
            <li>✗ You want to be different — Marines are everywhere</li>
            <li>✗ You want a horde army with lots of cheap models</li>
            <li>✗ You want aliens, chaos, or undead robots</li>
            <li>✗ You want maximum melee brutality (look at Orks or Berzerkers)</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- Chapter Choice -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16 bg-[#0d0d0f]">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-2">Pick your Chapter first</h2>
      <p class="text-[#8a8590] mb-8 text-lg">
        This is the most important decision. Your Chapter determines your colors, your lore, 
        and your playstyle. Pick with your gut — you'll be painting these for a while.
      </p>

      <div class="space-y-4">
        {[
          {
            name: 'Ultramarines',
            color: 'Royal Blue',
            swatch: 'bg-blue-700',
            playstyle: 'Tactical flexibility',
            painting: 'Easy',
            paintColor: 'text-green-400',
            desc: 'The default Space Marine. Disciplined, methodical, by-the-book. Blue armor with gold trim. The most tutorials exist for this scheme — great for beginners.',
          },
          {
            name: 'Blood Angels',
            color: 'Deep Red',
            swatch: 'bg-red-700',
            playstyle: 'Aggressive melee',
            painting: 'Easy–Medium',
            paintColor: 'text-yellow-400',
            desc: 'Noble warriors with a dark secret — a flaw in their gene-seed that can drive them to berserk fury. Beautiful red armor. Strong melee bonuses in rules.',
          },
          {
            name: 'Dark Angels',
            color: 'Dark Green / Black',
            swatch: 'bg-green-900',
            playstyle: 'Ranged firepower',
            painting: 'Easy',
            paintColor: 'text-green-400',
            desc: 'Secretive and brooding. Unforgiven for a betrayal ten thousand years ago. Dark green armor that hides easily in shadow. Strong Devastator and veteran units.',
          },
          {
            name: 'Space Wolves',
            color: 'Grey-Blue',
            swatch: 'bg-slate-500',
            playstyle: 'Aggressive melee + shooting',
            painting: 'Medium',
            paintColor: 'text-yellow-400',
            desc: 'Viking warriors in space who ride giant wolves. Loud, fierce, proud. Grey armor with lots of fur and bone details. More personality, slightly more complexity to paint.',
          },
          {
            name: 'Imperial Fists',
            color: 'Yellow',
            swatch: 'bg-yellow-500',
            playstyle: 'Siege and shooting',
            painting: 'Hard',
            paintColor: 'text-red-400',
            desc: 'Stubborn defenders and master siege warriors. Iconic yellow armor — but yellow is notoriously difficult to paint evenly. Not recommended for complete beginners.',
          },
        ].map(chapter => (
          <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-5">
            <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
              <div class={`w-4 h-full min-h-[48px] rounded ${chapter.swatch} flex-shrink-0`}></div>
              <div class="flex-1">
                <div class="flex items-center flex-wrap gap-3 mb-1">
                  <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-lg">{chapter.name}</h3>
                  <span class="text-xs text-[#4a4855]">{chapter.color}</span>
                  <span class={`text-xs font-semibold ${chapter.paintColor}`}>Painting: {chapter.painting}</span>
                </div>
                <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-xs mb-2">Playstyle: {chapter.playstyle}</p>
                <p class="text-[#b8b4c0] text-sm leading-relaxed">{chapter.desc}</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>

      <p class="text-[#4a4855] text-sm mt-6 italic">
        There are hundreds of other Chapters — these are the most common starter picks. 
        You can also invent your own Chapter with custom colors and rules.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- Painting -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-2">How to paint Space Marines</h2>
      <p class="text-[#8a8590] mb-8 text-lg">
        Using Ultramarines as the example — the easiest chapter for beginners. 
        The approach works for any chapter; just swap the color.
      </p>

      <div class="space-y-4 mb-10">
        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">1</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Spray with Macragge Blue (or your chapter color)</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Citadel's blue spray primer. Covers everything in one pass. For Blood Angels use Mephiston Red, for Dark Angels use Death World Forest.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">2</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Wash with Nuln Oil</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Apply over the whole model. Flows into panel lines and joints to create instant depth. Let it dry completely before moving on.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">3</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Layer the raised armor panels</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">For Ultramarines: Calgar Blue on the raised surfaces, avoiding the recesses. You're restoring the base color while the wash stays in the shadows.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">4</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Base coat the gold trim</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Retributor Armour on the shoulder pad rims, chest eagle, and knee pads. This is the detail that makes Marines look finished.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">5</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Paint the bolter black, pick out lenses</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Abaddon Black on the weapon casing. For eye lenses: a tiny dot of Moot Green or Averland Sunset — pick one color and stay consistent.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">6</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Base the model</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Astrogranite Debris texture paint, drybrush Administratum Grey over it, add a tuft. Done.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Contrast shortcut -->
      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#c9a84c] rounded-lg p-5">
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold mb-2">The even faster way: Contrast paints</h3>
        <p class="text-[#b8b4c0] text-sm leading-relaxed">
          Spray <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">Wraithbone</strong> (cream base coat), 
          then apply <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">Ultramarines Blue Contrast</strong> over the armor 
          in one pass. It self-shades and creates depth automatically. Then just add gold trim and 
          a black weapon. Entire Marine done in 15 minutes. 
          The result won't win awards but looks great on a table.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- What to buy -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16 bg-[#0d0d0f]">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-2">What to buy first</h2>
      <p class="text-[#8a8590] mb-10 text-lg">Start with the Combat Patrol. Paint it before buying anything else.</p>

      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#c9a84c] rounded-lg p-6 mb-6">
        <div class="mb-4">
          <span class="bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] text-xs font-semibold px-2 py-0.5 rounded font-display mr-2">Start Here</span>
          <span class="text-xs text-[#4a4855]">~$160</span>
        </div>
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-xl mb-2">Combat Patrol: Space Marines</h3>
        <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm mb-4 leading-relaxed">
          Includes a Captain in Terminator Armour, a Librarian in Terminator Armour, 
          5 Terminators, and 5 Infernus Marines. A heavily armoured Terminator-focused 
          force — durable, hard-hitting, and a great showcase of the Chapter's elite infantry.
        </p>
        <a
          href="https://www.games-workshop.com/en-US/Space-Marine-Combat-Patrol"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
          class="inline-block bg-[#c9a84c] hover:bg-[#dfc070] text-[#111113] font-semibold px-5 py-2.5 rounded text-sm transition-colors font-display"
        >
          Buy from Games Workshop →
        </a>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-6 mb-6">
        <div class="mb-3">
          <span class="text-xs text-[#4a4855]">~$65 · first expansion</span>
        </div>
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-xl mb-2">Primaris Intercessors (10-model box)</h3>
        <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm mb-4 leading-relaxed">
          The core troop of a Space Marine army. Durable, reliable, and satisfying to paint. 
          Adding a second squad gives you more bodies to hold objectives — the most important 
          thing in competitive 40k.
        </p>
        <a
          href="https://www.games-workshop.com/en-US/Primaris-Intercessors"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
          class="inline-block border border-[#2a2a35] hover:border-[#c9a84c] text-[#b8b4c0] hover:text-[#c9a84c] font-semibold px-5 py-2.5 rounded text-sm transition-colors font-display"
        >
          View on Games Workshop →
        </a>
      </div>

      <!-- Paints -->
      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-6">
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-xl mb-4">Paints you need (Ultramarines)</h3>
        <div class="space-y-3">
          {[
            { name: 'Macragge Blue Spray', use: 'Base coat — armor color', required: true },
            { name: 'Nuln Oil', use: 'Shade wash — depth and shadow', required: true },
            { name: 'Calgar Blue', use: 'Layer — restore raised armor panels', required: true },
            { name: 'Retributor Armour', use: 'Gold trim on shoulders, chest, knees', required: true },
            { name: 'Abaddon Black', use: 'Weapons and black areas', required: true },
            { name: 'Moot Green', use: 'Eye lenses — one dot per eye', required: false },
          ].map(paint => (
            <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class={`text-xs px-2 py-0.5 rounded mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0 font-display ${paint.required ? 'bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113]' : 'border border-[#2a2a35] text-[#4a4855]'}`}>
                {paint.required ? 'Essential' : 'Optional'}
              </span>
              <div>
                <span class="text-sm font-semibold">{paint.name}</span>
                <span class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm"> — {paint.use}</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
        <p class="text-[#4a4855] text-sm mt-4 italic">Different chapter? Swap Macragge Blue for your chapter's color. Everything else stays the same.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- Cost breakdown -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-8">Honest cost breakdown</h2>
      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg overflow-hidden">
        {[
          { item: 'Combat Patrol: Space Marines', cost: '~$160', note: 'Playable army out of one box' },
          { item: 'Essential paints (5)', cost: '~$30', note: 'Spray + shade + layer + gold + black' },
          { item: 'Basing supplies', cost: '~$12', note: 'Texture paint + tuft + grey' },
          { item: 'Clippers + hobby knife', cost: '~$20', note: 'One-time purchase' },
          { item: 'Superglue', cost: '~$5', note: 'Or plastic glue — both work' },
        ].map((row, i) => (
          <div class={`flex items-start justify-between px-5 py-4 gap-4 ${i % 2 === 0 ? '' : 'bg-[#111113]'}`}>
            <div>
              <p class="text-sm font-semibold">{row.item}</p>
              <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] mt-0.5">{row.note}</p>
            </div>
            <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] flex-shrink-0">{row.cost}</span>
          </div>
        ))}
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between px-5 py-4 bg-[#1f1d14] border-t border-[#c9a84c]">
          <p class="font-display font-semibold">All-in starter total</p>
          <span class="font-display font-bold text-[#c9a84c] text-lg">~$227</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="text-[#4a4855] text-sm mt-4 italic">
        Prices approximate. Chapter-specific spray colors vary — check availability before ordering.
        Wraithbone + Contrast paint is a cheaper alternative to the spray + layer approach.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="px-6 py-20 text-center">
    <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold mb-4">For the Emperor.</h2>
      <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-lg mb-8">
        Pick your Chapter. Grab the Combat Patrol. Start with five models before committing to the whole box.
        The painting journey is as much the point as the game.
      </p>
      <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 justify-center">
        <a
          href="/painting"
          class="inline-block bg-[#c9a84c] hover:bg-[#dfc070] text-[#111113] font-semibold px-8 py-4 rounded text-lg transition-colors font-display tracking-wide"
        >
          Painting Guide →
        </a>
        <a
          href="/quiz"
          class="inline-block border border-[#2a2a35] hover:border-[#c9a84c] text-[#b8b4c0] hover:text-[#c9a84c] font-semibold px-8 py-4 rounded text-lg transition-colors font-display"
        >
          Retake the Quiz
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>
